Changes to the NIST software (per the NIST notice)
--------------------------------------------------
2026, EPI Quantum Crypto team:
  - Port of the C++11 code base to C99 (include/*.h): estimators of
    SP 800-90B sections 5 and 6.3, restart and conditioning computations.
  - New library API (include/sp80090b.h, src/sp80090b_api.c) replacing the
    ea_iid, ea_non_iid, ea_restart and ea_conditioning executables: in-memory
    buffers, options and result structures, return codes and warnings.
  - Removal of the jsoncpp, GMP, MPFR and OpenSSL dependencies.
  - Thread-local state for concurrent assessments; OpenMP parallelisation kept.
  - Self-test tolerance tightened from 1e-6 to 1e-10 (selftest/compareresults.pl).
  - New programs: test_* (src/), labs and dataset generator (lab/).

Third-party components
----------------------
  - Cephes Mathematical Library, Copyright 1984, 1995, 2000 by Stephen L. Moshier
    (functions in include/chi_square_tests.h, as in the NIST tool).
  - Linked at build time, not distributed: libdivsufsort (Y. Mori, MIT License),
    libbz2 (bzip2, BSD-style license), libgomp (GCC runtime library exception).
  - lab/jent_record.c uses, but does not include, the Jitter RNG
    (jitterentropy-library, S. Mueller), obtained separately (JENT_SRC).
  - bin/ and selftest/refdata/: reference datasets and outputs of the NIST tool.
